<title>EGYPT: Yield falls on Egyptian 91-day T-bills.</title>
<headline>Yield falls on Egyptian 91-day T-bills.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on Egyptian 91-day treasury bills fell to 8.816 percent at Wednesday's auction from 8.921 percent at the previous auction on June 25.</p>
<p>The Central Bank of Egypt had asked for 600 million pounds and accepted bids for 676.750 million. Bills worth 673.100 million pounds mature on Thursday.</p>
<p>The Central Bank announced the following details (values in pounds, previous auction in brackets):</p>
<p>Maturity date: Oct 2, 1997 (Sept 25, 1997)</p>
<p>Average yield: 8.816 percent (8.921)</p>
<p>Value of bids accepted: 676.750 million (1,248.000 million)</p>
<p>Value of bids: 1,180.375 million (1.661.425 million)</p>
<p>Range accepted: 8.545 - 8.876 percent (8.600 - 8.951)</p>
<p>Range of bids: 8.545 - 10.002 percent (8.600 - 10.002)</p>
<p>Number of bids accepted: 62 (51)</p>
<p>Number of bids: 114 (91)</p>
<p>$1 = 3.395 pounds</p>
<p>-- Cairo reporting unit +20 2 578 3290/1 jw</p>
